{"id": "opportunities-for-all-jcyc", "title": "Opportunities for All: $5.6M in stipends paid with no proof of work", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.075, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "3aa4920f2d1ef4e7", "words": 375, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[9]"], "text": "In 2018, Mayor London Breed launched Opportunities for All: paid internships for young San Franciscans.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 6.48, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Opportunities for All", "sub": "launched by Mayor London Breed, October 2018"}, "emph": ["paid internships"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.28, 0.95, 1.18, 1.49, 1.84, 2.16, 2.98, 3.22, 3.93, 4.16, 4.74, 4.89, 5.13, 5.34]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The Human Rights Commission, under director Sheryl Davis, ran it.", "t0": 6.6, "t1": 9.75, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Children, Youth and Their Families", "sub": "held the grant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "ran it, under Sheryl Davis"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "sub": "paid the interns"}], "kicker": "Opportunities for All"}, "emph": ["Sheryl Davis"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.27, 0.49, 1.09, 1.33, 1.77, 2.17, 2.68, 2.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "A Japantown nonprofit, the Japanese Community Youth Council, paid the interns.", "t0": 9.87, "t1": 14.17, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Children, Youth and Their Families", "sub": "held the grant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "ran it, under Sheryl Davis"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "sub": "paid the interns"}], "kicker": "Opportunities for All"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.6, 1.38, 1.47, 1.85, 2.29, 2.52, 3.26, 3.46, 3.59]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "In the pandemic, it paid flat stipends instead of wages.", "t0": 14.29, "t1": 17.34, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Stipends instead of wages", "sub": "fiscal 2020-21 to 2022-23"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.16, 0.68, 0.81, 1.0, 1.37, 1.94, 2.29, 2.43]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "How much was paid with no proof of work?", "t0": 17.46, "t1": 19.45, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Stipends instead of wages", "sub": "fiscal 2020-21 to 2022-23"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.51, 0.78, 0.97, 1.17, 1.44, 1.55]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]", "amount"], "text": "About 5.4 million dollars.", "t0": 19.45, "t1": 22.38, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5,358,870", "label": "in stipends, no record of eligibility or work", "sub": "the audit’s summary gives $5.6 million and does not show how the two differ"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.04, 0.6, 0.91, 1.31, 1.52, 2.26]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["sources", "status"], "text": "That’s an official finding, from the City Controller’s audit in August 2026.", "t0": 22.9, "t1": 27.6, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "An official finding", "sub": "Controller’s audit, 26 Aug 2026, 27 recommendations"}, "emph": ["official finding"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.28, 0.66, 1.37, 1.46, 1.62, 1.84, 2.38, 2.77, 2.99, 3.48, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "The nonprofit paid from spreadsheets the Commission sent.", "t0": 27.82, "t1": 30.61, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no timesheets, no eligibility checks"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.68, 1.01, 1.19, 1.84, 1.98, 2.32]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "No timesheets, no eligibility checks. And 14 of 20 sampled expenses couldn’t be supported.", "t0": 30.73, "t1": 36.98, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no timesheets, no eligibility checks"}, "emph": ["14 of 20"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.94, 1.08, 1.62, 2.25, 2.6, 3.3, 3.56, 4.0, 4.45, 5.05, 5.6, 5.7]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "innocent[1]"], "text": "How could that happen?", "t0": 37.1, "t1": 38.21, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Children, Youth and Their Families", "sub": "held the grant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "ran it, under Sheryl Davis"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "sub": "paid the interns"}], "kicker": "Opportunities for All"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "innocent[1]"], "text": "One office decided who got paid, another held the grant, a third wrote the cheques.", "t0": 38.21, "t1": 43.35, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Children, Youth and Their Families", "sub": "held the grant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "ran it, under Sheryl Davis"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "sub": "paid the interns"}], "kicker": "Opportunities for All"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.64, 0.95, 1.36, 1.47, 1.71, 2.28, 2.65, 2.85, 2.98, 3.76, 3.86, 4.23, 4.56, 4.65]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "innocent[1]"], "text": "Nobody answered for all three.", "t0": 43.47, "t1": 45.22, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Children, Youth and Their Families", "sub": "held the grant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Human Rights Commission", "sub": "ran it, under Sheryl Davis"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "sub": "paid the interns"}], "kicker": "Opportunities for All"}, "emph": ["Nobody"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.89, 1.04, 1.21]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The Commission told the public 2,995 young people took part in the first two summers.", "t0": 45.44, "t1": 51.42, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["HRC reported, summers 2019 and 2020", "2,995"], "b": ["JCYC pay records support", "1,009"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.41, 0.61, 0.72, 1.11, 1.37, 1.79, 2.19, 2.54, 3.39, 3.69, 4.07, 4.35, 4.58, 4.72, 4.88, 5.18, 5.41]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Pay records support 1,009.", "t0": 51.54, "t1": 53.65, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["HRC reported, summers 2019 and 2020", "2,995"], "b": ["JCYC pay records support", "1,009"]}, "emph": ["1,009"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.58, 0.97, 1.19, 1.68]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[9]"], "text": "Meanwhile, the grant grew from about 2 million dollars to 13.3 million.", "t0": 53.77, "t1": 58.33, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["DCYF grant, 2019", "$1,958,000"], "b": ["after amendments", "$13.3 million"]}, "emph": ["13.3 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.59, 0.83, 1.1, 1.28, 1.63, 1.79, 2.16, 2.59, 2.84, 3.39, 3.85, 4.03]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "Who managed the program day to day? An outside consultant. Davis’s sister.", "t0": 58.55, "t1": 62.59, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The program manager", "kicker": "Who ran it", "sub": "an outside consultant: the director’s sister"}, "emph": ["sister"], "wt": [0.04, 0.1, 0.38, 0.49, 0.92, 1.08, 1.24, 1.65, 1.8, 2.18, 2.9, 3.6]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The nonprofit says Davis asked it to hire her, and private money paid her.", "t0": 62.71, "t1": 66.55, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Her contract", "kicker": "Withheld from the auditors", "stamp": "withheld"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.63, 0.87, 1.23, 1.53, 1.65, 1.76, 2.05, 2.46, 2.57, 2.94, 3.25, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "But it wouldn’t show auditors her contract. So none of that could be checked.", "t0": 66.67, "t1": 69.82, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Her contract", "kicker": "Withheld from the auditors", "stamp": "withheld"}, "emph": ["wouldn’t"], "wt": [0.0, 0.0, 0.06, 0.35, 0.53, 0.96, 1.13, 1.86, 1.99, 2.14, 2.23, 2.43, 2.58, 2.69]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "The criminal case against Davis adds more.", "t0": 70.04, "t1": 72.17, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Going Public PR", "kicker": "The criminal case", "sub": "a contract to promote Davis herself, 2022", "chip": "$10,000 from JCYC"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.37, 0.65, 0.97, 1.34, 1.65]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "Prosecutors say the nonprofit paid 10,000 dollars toward Going Public PR, hired to promote her.", "t0": 72.29, "t1": 78.04, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Going Public PR", "kicker": "The criminal case", "sub": "a contract to promote Davis herself, 2022", "chip": "$10,000 from JCYC"}, "emph": ["10,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.67, 0.83, 1.36, 1.65, 1.87, 2.31, 2.68, 3.0, 3.36, 3.85, 4.7, 4.97, 5.07, 5.45]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]", "established[5]"], "text": "On her own disclosure form, she named the program’s donor,", "t0": 78.16, "t1": 81.27, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Crankstart/Opportunities for All: travel, $1,214"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.28, 0.49, 0.95, 1.4, 1.61, 1.9, 2.06, 2.51]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]", "established[5]"], "text": "Crankstart, for 1,214 dollars of travel.", "t0": 81.27, "t1": 85.37, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Crankstart/Opportunities for All: travel, $1,214"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.96, 1.17, 1.32, 1.73, 1.99, 2.31, 2.91, 3.41, 3.57]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]", "established[5]"], "text": "Prosecutors say Collective Impact paid.", "t0": 85.49, "t1": 87.33, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Crankstart/Opportunities for All: travel, $1,214"}, "emph": ["Collective Impact"], "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 0.66, 1.05, 1.43]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "The program’s donations were banked at Collective Impact, a City grantee.", "t0": 87.45, "t1": 91.01, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Crankstart Foundation", "sub": "gave to the program"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Collective Impact", "sub": "banked the donations"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Davis’s travel", "sub": "reported as Crankstart’s"}], "kicker": "Where the donations went"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.5, 1.0, 1.16, 1.51, 1.6, 2.0, 2.64, 2.71, 2.89]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "So naming the donor kept that grantee off her form.", "t0": 91.13, "t1": 93.77, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Crankstart Foundation", "sub": "gave to the program"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Collective Impact", "sub": "banked the donations"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Davis’s travel", "sub": "reported as Crankstart’s"}], "kicker": "Where the donations went"}, "emph": ["off her form"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 0.52, 0.89, 1.14, 1.26, 1.85, 2.06, 2.24]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["defense[3]"], "text": "Mission Local reported Davis pleaded not guilty. A charge is an allegation, not a conviction.", "t0": 93.89, "t1": 99.59, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A charge is an allegation, not a conviction."}, "emph": ["not guilty"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.47, 1.01, 1.43, 1.85, 2.2, 3.17, 3.31, 3.71, 3.79, 3.88, 4.77, 4.92, 5.0]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "And the nonprofit is still the contractor.", "t0": 99.81, "t1": 102.12, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.03 million", "label": "paid to JCYC on the program since FY2025", "sub": "$7.6 million of it in FY2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.2, 0.9, 1.15, 1.43, 1.6]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "Since 2025, the City has paid it 19.03 million dollars.", "t0": 102.24, "t1": 107.36, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.03 million", "label": "paid to JCYC on the program since FY2025", "sub": "$7.6 million of it in FY2026"}, "emph": ["19.03 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.45, 1.18, 1.29, 1.55, 1.65, 1.88, 2.04, 2.56, 2.92, 3.16, 3.55, 4.22]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "established[8]"], "text": "The audit doesn’t find that anyone misused the stipends, or that the young people didn’t take part.", "t0": 107.48, "t1": 112.12, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That anyone misused the stipend money", "That the young people did not take part", "How JCYC handled private donations"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.29, 0.6, 0.81, 0.99, 1.46, 1.99, 2.1, 2.86, 3.04, 3.18, 3.26, 3.43, 3.8, 4.1, 4.32]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "established[8]"], "text": "It finds the records weren’t kept.", "t0": 112.24, "t1": 114.04, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That anyone misused the stipend money", "That the young people did not take part", "How JCYC handled private donations"]}, "emph": ["weren’t kept"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.41, 0.54, 1.09, 1.48]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[10]", "defense[0]"], "text": "The Commission’s new agency agrees with the audit.", "t0": 114.16, "t1": 116.48, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Agency for Human Rights", "agrees with the audit"], "b": ["JCYC", "disputes any misuse"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.02, 0.47, 0.67, 1.25, 1.66, 1.79, 1.9]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[10]", "defense[0]"], "text": "The nonprofit’s director, Jon Osaki, told The San Francisco Standard it paid on the City’s instructions.", "t0": 116.6, "t1": 122.28, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Agency for Human Rights", "agrees with the audit"], "b": ["JCYC", "disputes any misuse"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.65, 1.26, 1.5, 2.29, 2.48, 2.6, 2.8, 3.18, 3.7, 4.03, 4.35, 4.42, 4.53, 4.9]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[4]"], "text": "What would settle it? The manager’s contract, and the nonprofit’s ledger of private donations.", "t0": 122.4, "t1": 127.16, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The program manager’s contract, and JCYC’s ledger of private donations"}, {"who": "", "what": "The Controller’s follow-up on the 27 recommendations"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.22, 0.5, 0.8, 0.93, 1.39, 2.24, 2.31, 2.43, 3.1, 3.56, 3.75, 4.08]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.28, "t1": 129.37, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.56, 0.7, 1.01, 1.13, 1.23, 1.45, 1.69]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "No timesheets", "lead2": "Two-thirds overstated", "lead3": "The director’s sister", "lead4": "The charges", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "timeline"}